data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` with `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** Both compiled and ran without issues:

```csharp
Span<nint> span = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> uspan = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

This works because `nint`/`nuint` (native-sized integers, introduced in C# 9) are unmanaged types, which is the only requirement for `stackalloc`. On this 64-bit system, `nint.Size` was 8 bytes, so the 5-element `nint` span allocated 40 bytes on the stack.
